"""Put the Dagric logo on a QML window's title bar, on X11.

    /usr/lib/dagric/set-window-icon dagric-firstrun &

WHY THIS EXISTS
---------------
The first-run wizard came up with a gold "W" — the Qt Quick runtime's own badge
— in its title bar and taskbar entry, on the first window a customer ever sees.

Half of that is fixed elsewhere: the wizard now launches through a symlink named
after itself, so its WM_CLASS is "dagric-firstrun", and Plasma's task manager
matches that to dagric-firstrun.desktop and uses Icon=dagric-logo. The taskbar
is correct.

The title bar is not, and cannot be fixed the same way. Qt's qml runtime calls
setWindowIcon() with a resource compiled into the binary, so the window carries
a real _NET_WM_ICON property, and a window manager always prefers that over any
.desktop lookup. Confirmed with xprop under Xvfb: _NET_WM_ICON(CARDINAL) = Icon
(64 x 64), already set, before we get a say.

QML cannot override it. Enumerating every property of Window, ApplicationWindow
and Qt.application at runtime turns up nothing containing "icon" — Qt 6 simply
does not expose the window icon to QML. So the only place left to change it is
the X server, after the window exists.

WHY IT IS WORTH DOING AT ALL, given the default session is Wayland (where app_id
already resolves to the right .desktop file and the icon is correct): the X11
session is what you get in VirtualBox, VMware and QEMU, and on older NVIDIA
hardware. Trying the OS in a VM is exactly how a cautious switcher evaluates it
before committing a machine — so the X11 path is not an edge case, it is the
first impression.

SAFETY
------
This runs detached, alongside the most important window in the product, so it is
written to fail silently and never to interfere:
  * every failure path returns quietly — no output, no non-zero exit that could
    surface in a log the owner reads
  * it gives up after a fixed deadline rather than waiting forever for a window
    that may never appear
  * it only ever writes one property on a window whose WM_CLASS we chose
  * on Wayland it exits immediately, because there is nothing to fix and no X
    server to talk to
The worst case is the title bar keeping the icon it has today.
"""

import os
import struct
import sys
import time

DEADLINE = 20.0          # seconds to wait for the window to appear
POLL = 0.25
BLOB = "/usr/share/dagric/icon/dagric-64.rgba"
SIDE = 64


def _quiet_exit():
    raise SystemExit(0)


def load_icon():
    """RGBA bytes -> the CARDINAL list _NET_WM_ICON wants.

    The property is width, height, then one 32-bit ARGB word per pixel. The
    blob is straight RGBA in file order, so each pixel is rotated here; doing
    the swap at runtime keeps tools/make-icon-blob.sh producing a plain,
    inspectable image file rather than something in X11's private word order.
    """
    with open(BLOB, "rb") as fh:
        raw = fh.read()
    if len(raw) != SIDE * SIDE * 4:
        return None
    out = [SIDE, SIDE]
    for i in range(0, len(raw), 4):
        r, g, b, a = raw[i], raw[i + 1], raw[i + 2], raw[i + 3]
        out.append((a << 24) | (r << 16) | (g << 8) | b)
    return out


def main():
    if len(sys.argv) < 2:
        _quiet_exit()
    wanted = sys.argv[1]

    # Wayland needs nothing from us and has no X server to talk to.
    if os.environ.get("XDG_SESSION_TYPE") == "wayland" or not os.environ.get("DISPLAY"):
        _quiet_exit()

    try:
        from Xlib import display, X
        from Xlib.error import XError
    except Exception:
        _quiet_exit()

    icon = load_icon()
    if not icon:
        _quiet_exit()

    try:
        dpy = display.Display()
    except Exception:
        _quiet_exit()

    root = dpy.screen().root
    net_icon = dpy.intern_atom("_NET_WM_ICON")
    cardinal = dpy.intern_atom("CARDINAL")

    def walk(win, depth=0):
        """Find every window whose WM_CLASS instance matches.

        Recursion is bounded: a toolkit reparents its window a few levels below
        the root at most, and an unbounded walk on a busy desktop is a lot of
        round trips for no gain.
        """
        found = []
        if depth > 4:
            return found
        try:
            cls = win.get_wm_class()
            if cls and wanted in cls:
                found.append(win)
            for child in win.query_tree().children:
                found.extend(walk(child, depth + 1))
        except (XError, Exception):
            pass
        return found

    deadline = time.time() + DEADLINE
    while time.time() < deadline:
        targets = walk(root)
        if targets:
            for win in targets:
                try:
                    win.change_property(net_icon, cardinal, 32, icon)
                except Exception:
                    pass
            try:
                dpy.sync()
            except Exception:
                pass
            _quiet_exit()
        time.sleep(POLL)
    _quiet_exit()


if __name__ == "__main__":
    try:
        main()
    except SystemExit:
        raise
    except Exception:
        # Never let a title-bar cosmetic fault produce a traceback next to the
        # first-run wizard.
        pass
